Configuration files:
it will have resource configuration.
here we write inputs for our resource
based on that input terraform will create the real world resources.
extension is ".tf"

first create a terraform folder/directory
mkdir terraform
Get into the folder
cd terraform
create main.tf

terraform code:-

provider "aws" {
    region="eu-north-1"
}

resource "aws_instance" "one" {
    ami="ami-0a716d3f3b16d290c"
    instance_type="t3.micro"
}

I-->init
P-->plan
A-->apply
D-->destroy

Terraform Commands:-
Terraform init:-Initialize the provider plugins on backend.It will store informations of plugin in .terraform folder.with-out plugins we can't create resource.
each provider will have its own plugin
we can get every provider from terraform registry
once plugins are downloaded we should not need to run init command every time.

PLUGINS:- Are Responsible to create resource in Cloud.

Terraform Plan:-To create an execution plan
it will take inputs given by users and plan the resource creation
if we haven't given inputs for few fields it will take default values

Terraform apply:-To create resources
as per the given inputs on configuration file it will create the resources in real world.

Terraform Destroy:-To delete resources.

provider "aws" {
    region= "eu-north-1"
}

resource "aws_instance" "One" {
    count=5
    ami="ami-03eb6185d756497f8"
    instance_type= "t3.micro"
}

terraform apply --auto-approve
terraform destroy --auto-approve

STATE FILE: Used to store the resource information which is created by terraform to track the resource activities.
in real time entire resource info is on state file.
we need to keep it safe & secure.
if we lost this file we can't track the infra.
Command:
terraform state list

terraform target:used to destroy the specific resource

Wanted to destroy single resource.
terraform destroy -auto-approve -target="aws_instance.one[1]"

Wanted to destroy multiple resources.
terraform destroy -auto-approve -target="aws_instance.one[1]" -target="aws_instance.one[2]"

